    "id": "p0",
    "title": "Longer Motions",
    "text": "Supers use longer motions, but you read them exactly like Specials: {input:214214} repeats a motion, {input:641236} sweeps through half the directions, and {input:2141236} chains two motions together. Roll through the directions smoothly and press the attack near the end. Long motions also come out more consistently when they end on a diagonal - {input:64123} registers {input:641236} cleanly."
   },
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "title": "Air Supers and SP",
    "text": "Some Supers work in the air too - Shiori's {input:2141236} Super has airborne versions. You've got free SP in this lesson so you can focus on the motions; in a real match, budget it like the SP lesson showed."
   }
